    ],
    "reading_order": 11,
    "text": "What does the photographer do when she prints photographs of different sizes\nfrom the same negative? You must  have heard about the stamp size, passport size and\npostcard size photographs. She generally takes a photograph on a small size film, say\nof 35mm size and then enlarges it into a bigger size, say 45mm (or 55mm). Thus, if we\nconsider any line segment in the smaller photograph (figure), its corresponding line",
    "latex": null,
